---
/**
 * The homepage hero's motion, design ref "1a · Calm Pulse" from the
 * "Final-Roars_4" handoff.
 *
 * It replaces the 5d WebGL field (`DitherHero variant="roar-wave"`) on the
 * HOMEPAGE ONLY. The inner pages keep their 3a `carbon-heat` header, which this
 * handoff says nothing about and which is not in its scope.
 *
 * The redesign answers one piece of feedback — the hero read as loud — and it
 * answers it by construction rather than by turning anything down. The rings
 * live in the right-hand ~45% of the frame, and every box marked `data-safe`
 * keeps a 36px dot-free pad with a 90px ramp out of it, so no mark is ever
 * behind the headline, the lead, the button or the labels. That is why the old
 * `inkStrength` easing has no equivalent here: the marks that were causing the
 * glare are not drawn at all now.
 *
 * NO GROUND AND NO GRAIN OF ITS OWN. The canvas is transparent and paints only
 * dots. The hero's yellow and GrainField's grain are untouched underneath —
 * the handoff generates a grain tile because its reference page has none, and
 * this hero already has one. Two grain layers would darken the ground, and a
 * second flat ground under a field is what produced the tonal seam on this site
 * three times before.
 *
 * The paint is in src/scripts/hero-pulse.ts, verbatim from the handoff.
 */
---

<canvas
  class="hp"
  aria-hidden="true"
  data-hero-pulse-canvas></canvas>

<style>
  /* Above the hero's ground, below its content, which sits at z-index 1.
     `.hero` is `isolation: isolate`, so these sort against each other rather
     than against the section. */
  .hp {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: 0;
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    /* The hero listens for nothing here and the copy under it must stay
       clickable: the CTA sits inside this box. */
    pointer-events: none;
  }
</style>

<script>
  import { initHeroPulse } from '../scripts/hero-pulse'
  initHeroPulse()
</script>
